<div class="note"><details><summary>What these numbers mean</summary><p><b>Active play:</b> at least 10 seconds of play plus movement beyond 5% of the route or a collected item. Time counts during visible gameplay and stops five seconds after the last game input; pauses, story reading and idle menus do not count.</p><p><b>Progress:</b> the furthest position reached on the chapter route, not a learning score. Scrolls show story discoveries (story moments in the 3D escape); stumbles include falls and encounters. Completion is reported by the game. Little Light receives basic objective checks; the 3D escape reports section arrival. Neither game’s movement is replayed on the server. Finish rate uses all chapter starts.</p><p><b>Browsers are not people.</b> A shared device can represent several players; one player can use several devices. These reports cannot confirm age or prove human identity, and automated clients can imitate play. No names, additional IP addresses, raw inputs, device fingerprints, or music filenames are collected by this feature.</p><p>Each restart, chapter switch, or page reload followed by play begins a new attempt. Only play after this update is measured. Reports arrive about every 15 seconds and at key transitions. Blocked tracking, lost connections, or an abrupt browser close can leave incomplete reports. Attempts are retained for 90 days.</p><p>Signed-in staff and <code>?preview=1</code> game visits are classified as tests. You can also mark an attempt as a test below.</p></details></div>
